To convert local coordinates to world coordinates in Unity, you can use the `Transform.TransformPoint` method. This method takes a vector in the local space of the transform and converts it to world space, accounting for the transform's position, rotation, and scale, as well as any parent transforms in the hierarchy.

Here is an example script demonstrating this process:

```csharp
using UnityEngine;

public class LocalToWorldExample : MonoBehaviour
{
    void Start()
    {
        // Define local position relative to this transform
        Vector3 localPosition = new Vector3(1, 2, 3);

        // Convert local position to world position
        Vector3 worldPosition = transform.TransformPoint(localPosition);

        // Output the world position
        Debug.Log("World Position: " + worldPosition);

        // Optional: Verify using localToWorldMatrix
        Vector3 worldPositionMatrix = transform.localToWorldMatrix.MultiplyPoint(localPosition);
        Debug.Log("World Position via Matrix: " + worldPositionMatrix);
    }
}
```

